<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan scraps 5,000-T basmati rice export tender.</title>
<headline>Pakistan scraps 5,000-T basmati rice export tender.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Rice Export Corporation of Pakistan (RECP) on Monday scrapped three bids for the sale and export of 5,000 tonnes of basmati variety Pak-7 1996/97 (July-June) rice containing seven percent broken.</p>
<p>An RECP official said the corporation felt the bids opened on May 26 were too low at $436 per tonne FOB, $435.10 and $425.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
